CMake: test if(QNX), not CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL QNX (which compares with the variable QNX's value).

HailoRT picks its QNX sources with if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL QNX).
CMake defines a variable QNX (1) when it targets QNX, and an unquoted
argument that names a variable is replaced by its value, so the test
compared "QNX" with "1" and was false: the Linux event, driver-scan and
PCIe sources were compiled instead of the QNX ones (eventfd/poll code that
does not build against QNX's pevents handles), and libhailort was not
linked with QNX's libpci. With these files' cmake_minimum_required(3.0)
policies even a quoted "QNX" is dereferenced (CMP0054 OLD), so the tests
use the QNX variable itself, as CMake intends: if(QNX), if(NOT QNX).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/hailort/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/hailort/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 add_subdirectory(external/DotWriter EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)
 add_subdirectory(external/spdlog EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)
 set_target_properties(spdlog PROPERTIES POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
-if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL QNX)
+if(QNX)
     add_library(pevents STATIC EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL external/pevents/src/pevents.cpp)
     target_include_directories(pevents PUBLIC external/pevents/src)
     target_compile_definitions(pevents PRIVATE -DWFMO)
--- a/hailort/hailortcli/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/hailort/hailortcli/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
 
 if(WIN32)
     target_link_libraries(hailortcli Ws2_32 Iphlpapi Shlwapi winmm.lib)
-elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL QNX)
+elseif(QNX)
     target_link_libraries(hailortcli pevents)
 endif()
 target_include_directories(hailortcli
